ook.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings.", "Incumbent Joe Wilson (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Joe Wilson, a Republican who has held this Columbia-area district since 2001, seeks another term against Zyon Khalifa, a 25-year-old political newcomer who secured the Democratic nomination through a June runoff. The district leans Republican by about seven points, and every major race rating places it in the Solid or Safe Republican column. Wilson has vastly out-raised Khalifa, roughly $861,000 to about $19,000, leaving the challenger with little cash for advertising in a media market that spans two states.\n\nNo public general-election polling is available, so the outlook rests on district fundamentals, ratings, and money. The Democratic national climate provides some background lift for Khalifa, and headline coverage of the race has been modest. Still, the combination of incumbency, district lean, and financial disparity makes Wilson a clear favorite, with Khalifa needing an unexpected shift to compete.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0664, "margin": -9.56}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0576, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0526, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0819, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0438, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0396, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0537, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0512, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0392, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.0515, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.0498, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.0541, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.0624, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.0587, "margin": -10.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.0236, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "20